  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-02-19T08:31:54.031Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Basically, it'd be nice to be able to simply load into an avatar and have it immediately work with fullbody instead of having to stop, T-Pose, align and click into it. Either binding the tracking points to the correct bones, or if that doesn't work well, allow users to drop in a script with a visible orb to the bone they plan to track and position it to their liking would completely eliminate that step altogether.\nGiven the scaling of TDA models' limbs, the latter is most likely a better option, but I don't know enough about fullbody to say, since I use Kinect and not physical based Vive fullbody.",
